  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Increased capacities of Saudi Arabia constituents to create enabling environment for cooperative entrepreneurship and sustainable enterprises</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In recent years, the Kingdom has been moving toward a sustainable and diversified economy, in line with the national priorities articulated in its Vision 2030, which calls for increased employment of nationals in the private sector, reduced unemployment rates among Saudis, and increased labour force participation rates of women. Efforts to achieve these goals entail supporting small and medium enterprise&apos;s development, including cooperatives. The country aims now to develop a National Cooperative Strategy to develop the sector followed by a new cooperatives law.  
Acknowledging the important role that cooperatives play and the need to foster cooperative development in KSA, the Kingdom requires support both at the policy and legal fronts, but also in terms of statistics, the latter deemed critical for evidence-based policy development, monitoring and evaluation. Institutions, including the Ministry of Human Resources and Social Development (MHRSD), and primary and secondary cooperatives, also require capacity-building support to enable them to effectively assume and strengthen their role in the cooperative&#x2019;s ecosystem in the Kingdom. 
Overall, developing and strengthening cooperative enterprises in the Kingdom is a priority area that should be guided and informed by international labour standards and instruments, as well as international best practices.</narrative>
  </description>
